		{
			"id": "109559763671705768",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez/109559763511858326",
			"author": {
				"name": "Philip (is looking for work)",
				"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/213/008/546/280/original/716603c4d65ea709.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2022-12-22T22:48:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The magic here is that rather than having to remember to explicitly compile each SCSS file (à la <a href=\"https://github.com/philiprenich/philiprenich.com/blob/main/.eleventy.js#L17\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/philiprenich/philip</span><span class=\"invisible\">renich.com/blob/main/.eleventy.js#L17</span></a> ) 11ty instead handles all that file gathering for you behind the scenes?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109559779792394483",
			"parentId": "109559763671705768",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109559779792394483",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-12-22T22:52:49.592Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.nz/@mez\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>mez</span></a></span> yeah, exactly. Any .scss file that doesn’t start with an underscore is compiled to your output folder via standard Eleventy file routing rules.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
